1
00:00:00,718 --> 00:00:03,318
(Sheldon:)who can't find love himself.

2
00:00:04,755 --> 00:00:06,925
(Sheldon:)It's ironic, but the point is

3
00:00:06,924 --> 00:00:08,454
(Sheldon:)we can't trust you.

4
00:00:08,459 --> 00:00:11,689
(Sheldon:)You're a sketchy character
in a parking garage.

5
00:00:11,695 --> 00:00:13,165
(Man:)Yeah, well,
from my perspective,

6
00:00:13,163 --> 00:00:14,663
(Man:)that's how you two appear to me.

7
00:00:14,665 --> 00:00:17,935
(Sheldon:)Well, I never thought
of it like that.

8
00:00:17,935 --> 00:00:21,435
(Sheldon:)Boy, frame of reference will
just sneak up on you, won't it?

9
00:00:22,606 --> 00:00:24,506
(Leonard:)My friend does make a decent
point about the money.

10
00:00:24,508 --> 00:00:26,878
(Leonard:)I don't feel comfortable
just handing it over up front.

11
00:00:26,877 --> 00:00:29,177
Ah-ah-ah, no money, no helium.

12
00:00:29,179 --> 00:00:32,579
(Man:)Seems we're at a, uh, stalemate.

13
00:00:32,583 --> 00:00:34,213
(Sheldon:)Not technically.

14
00:00:34,218 --> 00:00:36,248
(Sheldon:)In chess, a stalemate
refers to a situation

15
00:00:36,253 --> 00:00:38,283
(Sheldon:)in which there
are no remaining moves.

16
00:00:38,288 --> 00:00:40,388
(Sheldon:)Uh, you have plenty
of moves available.

17
00:00:40,390 --> 00:00:42,790
(Sheldon:)You could beat us up
and steal the money.

18
00:00:43,761 --> 00:00:46,061
(Sheldon:)You could kill us,
you know.

19
00:00:46,063 --> 00:00:50,203
(Sheldon:)Really, you're only limited
by your imagination.

20
00:00:51,535 --> 00:00:52,765
(Sheldon:)Huh.

21
00:00:52,770 --> 00:00:54,470
(Man:)All these years,
I've been using “stalemate,”

22
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:56,541
when I really mean “impasse.”

23
00:00:56,540 --> 00:01:01,020
(Man:)I feel foolish.

